 %3d/368  Skill Points  %3d/293  Wisdom Points   %3d/358  Soul Points	 %3d/368  技能點數  %3d/293  智慧點數   %3d/358  靈魂點數
Would you like to:	你希望：
    My lord King, look upon your stronghold, Camelot. By strength of spirit, skill of sword and quickness of mind, you have built a kingdom that could live in legends.	    吾王，且看你的要塞——肯萊特城堡。你以堅毅的心志、精湛的劍術與敏捷的智謀，締造了一個足以名留傳奇的王國。
    Beneath your firm and wise hand, the warring tribes of Celts, Saxons, Jutes, and Angles have been brought under control and foreign marauders driven from the shores.	    在你堅定睿智的治理之下，凱爾特人、撒克遜人、朱特人與盎格魯人這些征戰不休的部族俱已臣服，外敵劫掠者也已被逐出海岸。
    Your queen is the beautiful Gwenhyver, who loves you and whom you love dearly. Yet you know that her deepest and most passionate love is reserved for your greatest knight, Sir Launcelot.	    你的王后，美麗的昆海兒，愛著你，你也深愛著她。然而你心知，她最深沉、最熱切的愛，卻留給了你麾下最傑出的騎士——蘭斯洛特爵士。
    And because Launcelot is chivalrous, brave and a true friend, you do nothing to bring harm to him or your queen. Instead, you suffer in silence.	    而蘭斯洛特為人豪俠、驍勇，又是你真摯的朋友，你不忍加害於他或你的王后，只能獨自默默承受這份苦楚。
    Sharing the Round Table with you are noble warriors of the realm: Launcelot, Kai, Ector, Gareth, Percival, Gawaine, Galahad and many others.	    與你同坐圓桌的，是這王國裡的高貴武士：蘭斯洛特、凱伊、艾克特、加雷斯、帕西法爾、高文、葛拉漢，以及其他許多人。
    And I? I am Merlin. Advisor, mentor and, as some would have it, wizard, though my true nature remains a secret known only to the ancient gods and me.	    至於我？我是梅林。你的顧問、導師，也有人稱我是巫師，但我真正的本相，唯有古老諸神與我自己知曉。
    I must speak to you now of dark truths: the forbidden love of Gwenhyver and Launcelot has cast a blight upon your soul. And in so doing, has put a curse upon your kingdom.	    此刻，我必須向你道出一則黑暗的真相：昆海兒與蘭斯洛特之間那段禁忌之愛，已在你的靈魂上投下陰影，也因此為你的王國招來了詛咒。
    The fruit has withered on the vine, grain dies of disease, while springs and wells turn foul. Your people cry out to you for a miracle.	    果實在藤上枯萎，穀物染病而死，泉水與井水俱已腐臭。你的子民正向你哭求奇蹟。
    A vision of the Holy Grail covered in a white cloth appeared to you in your time of need. Three of your greatest knights went forth to seek it...	    就在你最需要指引之時，一幅覆著白布的聖杯異象，在你眼前顯現。你麾下三位最傑出的騎士，隨即啟程尋找它……
...Sir Gawaine...	……高文爵士……
...Sir Launcelot...	……蘭斯洛特爵士……
...and Sir Galahad.	……以及葛拉漢爵士。
    Gawaine, Launcelot and Galahad have not returned. The search must now fall to you and during this search you will be sorely tested in physical, moral and spiritual strength.	    高文、蘭斯洛特與葛拉漢至今未歸。如今，這場尋找必須落到你的肩上，而在尋找途中，你的體魄、道德與心靈之力都將受到嚴酷的考驗。
    If you are found wanting in any of these virtues, the Grail will be denied to you and your kingdom will turn to ashes and dust.	    若你在這些德行中有任何一項有所欠缺，聖杯將棄你而去，你的王國也將化為灰燼與塵土。
    I will watch over you and speak to you, though I will be with you only in spirit, not body.	    我將守護著你、與你交談，儘管伴隨你的只有我的心神，而非我的軀體。
    Prepare well, Arthur, for once you begin, you dare not turn back. Seek the Holy Grail! Search with all speed and dedication. Time is running out.	    亞瑟，做好萬全準備，因為此行一旦啟程，便再無回頭之路。去尋找聖杯！以最快的速度、最堅定的心意去尋找。時間所剩無多。
The forest and undergrowth are too thick to go that way.	林木與灌叢過於濃密，無法從那個方向通行。
I do not have the ability to look inside a solid tree.  I doubt that you have.	我沒有透視實心樹木的能力，我想你也沒有。
The forest grows thicker and darker.  It is impossible to see very far.	森林愈發濃密昏暗，視線難及遠方。
There are roots under the trees.	樹下有盤結的樹根。
Most of them are too tall for that.	多數樹木對此而言都太高了。
Aye, 'tis a forest and therefore filled with trees.	正是，此地乃森林，自然林木遍布。
Overhead is a thick canopy of leaves and interwoven branches filled with dappled light.	頭頂是濃密交織的枝葉華蓋，篩落點點斑駁的光影。
Trees are generally adorned with leaves.  Indeed, the trees here are quite thick with them.	樹木本就綴滿枝葉，此地的樹木更是枝葉茂密。
Most trees of my acquaintance have roots.  They are no threat to you, unless you are particularly clumsy.	依我所知，樹木大多都有根。它們對你並無威脅，除非你格外笨拙。
It is too thick to see through.	過於濃密，無法看穿。
The undergrowth of this forest protects many animals, but is the bane of travelers.	此地的灌木叢庇護著眾多野獸，卻是旅人的剋星。
The rich forest floor is covered with centuries of fallen leaves and thick grasses which muffle the sound of your passage.	肥沃的林地覆滿數百年堆積的落葉與濃密的野草，讓你行走的腳步聲悄然無聲。
It is a thick, hardy type of wild grass.	這是一種濃密而耐生的野草。
The only thing you would find under these stones is forest soil and a few worms perhaps.	在這些石頭底下，你只會找到林地的泥土，或許還有幾條蟲子。
There is much good stone in the forest, though some stones are more dangerous than others.	森林裡有不少好石頭，不過有些石頭比其他的更為危險。
There are only glimpses of the sky through the thick canopy of leaves overhead.	透過頭頂濃密的枝葉華蓋，只能瞥見片片天光。
It should not surprise you to see your knees, saddle and horse.	看見自己的膝蓋、馬鞍與坐騎，應該不會讓你感到意外。
There is nothing more exciting to see than your own booted feet.	沒有什麼比看著自己那雙穿靴的腳更令人興奮的了。
Aside from some very ordinary beetles, there is nothing of interest there.	除了幾隻極為普通的甲蟲，那裡沒有什麼值得留意的。
Once it was a tree, now it is a log.  Someday, it will be peat.  Such is the cycle of life.	它曾是一棵樹，如今成了朽木。終有一日，它將化為泥炭。生命的循環，便是如此。
Forget the beetles.  Think about your sacred mission.	別管那些甲蟲了，想想你神聖的使命吧。
There are no berries in the Forest Perilous.  Or certainly none you would dare to eat.	派瑞樂斯森林裡沒有漿果，至少沒有你敢吃的那種。
There are none here, but avoid the forest mushrooms at all costs.	這裡沒有，但無論如何都要避開林中的蕈菇。
They hear you and smell you and stay well away.	牠們聽見你、嗅到你的氣味，便遠遠避開了。
The birds are all but invisible in the dense trees.	鳥兒隱身在濃密的林木間，幾乎難見蹤影。
He looks much the same as he did a moment ago.	他看起來和方才並無二致。
What horse?	什麼馬？
He is part of the spirit of the forest and dwells in the heart of it.  You will not see him here.	他是森林精魄的一部分，棲居於林心之中，你在此處是見不到他的。
There are prints of your horse heading toward Camelot.  You may assume he is safe.	地上有你坐騎的蹄印，朝著肯萊特的方向而去。你可以斷定牠平安無事。
Gawaine will never be seen upon this earth again.	高文再也不會出現在這世間了。
Have you not seen enough boars for one quest?	難道這一趟任務裡，你見到的野豬還不夠多嗎？
The giant boars of the Forest Perilous are particularly dangerous.  How fortunate there are none around at the moment.	派瑞樂斯森林裡的巨型野豬格外危險。所幸此刻附近一頭也沒有。
You would need chisels for that.  You do not have time to play at being a stonemason.	那需要鑿子才行。你沒有閒工夫扮演石匠。
Your mule does not answer.	你的騾子沒有回應。
It is not edible.  Nor does it look appetizing.	它不能吃，看起來也毫無食欲。
It smells of green growing things, of musty mouldering things beneath the earth, of ash and oak, the passage of wolf and bear, squirrel and hare -- a thousand mingled scents of life and decay.	空氣中瀰漫著青翠草木的氣息，混著地底腐朽發霉之物，還有梣木與橡木、狼與熊、松鼠與野兔行過的痕跡——生與滅的萬千氣味交織在一起。
Almost impossible to do unless you have a net and many helpers.  Which you do not.	除非你有網子與眾多幫手，否則幾乎不可能辦到。而你兩者皆無。
There is no-one here to help.	這裡沒有人可以幫忙。
There is the rush of wind through the leaves, the scurry and scitter of the squirrels and small creatures, the bell-like notes of the birds.  The creaking of your leather and metallic jingle of your gear sets you apart from this forest world.	風穿過枝葉發出陣陣呼嘯，松鼠與小獸窸窸窣窣地竄動，鳥鳴清脆如鈴。而你身上皮革的吱嘎聲與裝備的金屬叮噹聲，卻讓你與這片森林的世界格格不入。
You could spend the rest of your life trying to cut your way through this forest.  Use your head and find the easiest path.	你就算耗盡餘生，也未必能砍出一條穿越這片森林的路。動動腦筋，找出最容易的那條路。
For that you want an axe and you have none.	要做那件事，你需要一把斧頭，而你並沒有。
You don't feel particularly inclined to climb trees.  Anyway, what do you expect if you did? A golden egg or a magick bird or something?	你並不特別想爬樹。再說，就算爬了，你又能指望什麼？一顆金蛋，還是一隻魔法鳥？
Rather like trying to ride the air, I would think.	我想，那大概就像試圖騎乘空氣一樣吧。
Is this some strange delusion you have that you are riding a horse, O' Arthur, King of all the Britons?	亞瑟，不列顛諸民之王啊，你莫非有種奇怪的錯覺，以為自己正騎著馬？
You have no time to spare for hunting.	你沒有時間可以耗在狩獵上。
The surviving boars have retreated far from this part of the forest.  They fear you now.	倖存的野豬已退到這片森林的遠處，牠們如今對你心生畏懼。
Face the giant boars only if you must.  They are the most deadly of the wild creatures here.	除非萬不得已，否則別去招惹那些巨型野豬。牠們是此地最致命的野獸。
I am sure you will find a likely tree when the need is great enough.	我相信，當真有必要時，你自會找到合適的樹。
From the deafening silence, I would say there are no talking stones here.	從這震耳欲聾的寂靜看來，此處應該沒有會說話的石頭。
This is not a talking tree.	這不是一棵會說話的樹。
I am already speaking.	我已經在說話了。
St. Leonard is long gone from his Forest and of no use to you.	聖倫納德早已離開他的森林，對你毫無用處。
The joys of hunting Windsor must wait for another time.	在溫莎狩獵的樂趣，得留待日後再說了。
There is nothing in ancient Avebury to help your search.	古老的埃夫伯里裡沒有任何東西能幫上你的尋找。
These silent stones of Mottistone have no tale to tell.	莫蒂斯通這些沉默的石頭，並無故事可說。
Let us hope you never have need of the healing waters of Bath.	但願你永遠用不上巴斯的療癒之泉。
St. Keyne of Keynsham has no connection with the Grail.	凱恩夏姆的聖凱恩，與聖杯毫無關聯。
The bishop of Winchester may be a miracle worker, but not even he knows where the Grail may be.	溫徹斯特的主教或許能行奇蹟，但就連他也不知道聖杯身在何處。
The martyrs of Shapwick provide no clue.	沙普維克的殉道者提供不了任何線索。
Avoid Halstock, where St. Juthware could not keep her head.	避開哈斯托克，聖朱斯瓦在那裡連自己的頭顱都保不住。
There is nothing of worth to milk from Braunton.	布朗頓沒有什麼值得你去汲取的東西。
Neither Hercules nor Hartland Point will lead to the Grail.	海克力斯與哈特蘭角，都不會指引你找到聖杯。
St. Sidwell's waters in Exeter will reveal nothing of use.	艾克希特的聖西德威爾之泉，不會透露任何有用的訊息。
Neither Brutus, his giants nor clue of the Grail are to be found in Totnes.	布魯特斯、他的巨人們，或是聖杯的線索，在托特尼斯都找不到。
It is made of the purest crystal, as best I can tell, and it contains enormous power such as only a wizard or enchantress could control.	依我看，它是以最純淨的水晶製成，蘊藏著巨大的力量，唯有巫師或女巫方能駕馭。
Such beings tend to manifest near some spot where they were once worshipped.	這類存在往往會在昔日受人崇拜之處現身。
They will not answer you now.	牠們此刻不會回應你。
You must find a place where they will answer you.	你必須找到一個牠們願意回應你的地方。
These walls are ancient and most likely would collapse beneath you.	這些牆垣年代久遠，你一踩上去多半會塌陷。
What a useless idea.	這主意毫無用處。
She is undoubtedly grazing at the bottom of the hill.	她想必正在山腳下吃草。
Not a trace of the Monk is left.  The Old Ones have taken him, body and soul.	僧侶已無蹤影可尋，古代幽靈已將他連同肉身與靈魂一併帶走。
If he is in these ruins, you will surely find him.	他若在這片廢墟之中，你必能找到他。
Are YOU mad?!  He is here!	你瘋了嗎？！他就在這裡！
You have the air of a man who is searching for someone, but I assure you I am the only other soul upon this Tor.	你身上帶著尋人的神情，但我向你保證，這座山丘上除了我，再無旁人。
He appears to be just on the other side of the wall.	他似乎就在牆的另一側。
There is little to be found but rubble.	這裡除了瓦礫，幾乎一無所有。
Inside the rubble is....nothing.	瓦礫之中……什麼也沒有。
It is only debris from the collapsed walls and roof of whatever once stood here.	這不過是此處昔日建物倒塌的牆垣與屋頂殘骸。
The sky is open overhead.  Not a bit of the original roof remains.	頭頂天空一片開闊，原本的屋頂已蕩然無存。
These could possibly be the ruins of the shrine built by Joseph of Arimathea, but no one, not even I, can be sure of that.	這裡或許就是亞利馬太的約瑟所建聖堂的遺跡，但無人能夠斷定——即便是我，也不敢肯定。
You have more important things to do.	你還有更重要的事得做。
It has been a sacred hill for centuries.	數百年來，這一直是座聖丘。
The Old Ones took his body and soul away.	古代幽靈把他的肉身與靈魂一併帶走了。
Perhaps the Monk no longer dwells here.  As yet, there is no sign of him.	或許那僧侶已不再住在此處，至今仍不見他的蹤影。
There is no monk in sight here.	這裡不見任何僧侶的蹤影。
Those glazed, fanatical eyes filled with hatred, those snarling lips flecked with foam!  The Monk truly is a madman!	那雙充滿仇恨、目光呆滯而狂熱的眼睛，那咆哮著、沾滿唾沫的雙唇！這僧侶果真是個瘋子！
Ah, so THIS is why he is called the Mad Monk of Glastonbury.	啊，原來這便是他被稱為格列斯登伯利瘋僧侶的緣由。
This Monk seems calm enough.  Perhaps he is not the one they call the Mad Monk.  We shall see.	這位僧侶看起來相當平靜。或許他並非人稱瘋僧侶的那一位。且看下去便知。
The spell of Circular Entrapment is broken now that you possess this crystal heart, for this was the object of power which held the spell in place.	如今你已擁有這顆水晶心，環困之咒已然破除，因為正是這件靈物維繫著這道咒語。
There is a spell of Circular Entrapment cast over Glastonbury Tor.  You cannot leave here unless you break it.	格列斯登伯利山上籠罩著一道環困之咒，除非破除它，否則你無法離開此地。
I sense only minor sorcerous ability in the monk, so there must be some other source of extraordinary power to hold the spell in place.	我只感應到這僧侶身上有些許微弱的法力，想必另有非凡的力量之源，維繫著這道咒語。
There are many illusions.  Some say life itself is an illusion.  But this is no time for philosophical discourse.	幻象有很多種。有人說生命本身便是一場幻象。但此刻並非高談哲理之時。
This monk has minor sorcerous powers, enough to generate two illusions of himself to confuse you.	這僧侶身懷些許法力，足以幻化出兩個自己的分身來迷惑你。
The illusions are harmless, but the monk is armed with a deadly club and can do you great harm indeed.	那些幻象並無害處，但僧侶手持一根致命的棍棒，確實能對你造成重創。
I do not know of any key.	我不知道有什麼鑰匙。
I know nothing of a crystal heart.  What a peculiar thing to ask about.	我對水晶心一無所知，你問這個還真是奇怪。
My heart is fine, thank you.	我的心很好，多謝關心。
Joseph of Arimathea is a legendary figure, supposedly a man who helped to bury Christ and who then brought the Grail to our island and established a shrine upon this Tor.	亞利馬太的約瑟是一位傳說人物，據說他曾協助安葬基督，其後將聖杯帶到我們這座島上，並在此山丘建立了一座聖堂。
Any doors this building once had are long gone.	這棟建築昔日或許有過門，但如今早已蕩然無存。
